  "description": "SLR Frameset\n\nTHE LATEST EVOLUTION OF OUR UNIQUE MASON SLR, WITH CONFIGURABLE SHIMANO BUILD OPTIONS\n\nThe MASON SLR steel modern super-tourer is the result of our focus on ride quality, long-distance performance, and luxury grand-touring capabilities. A new chapter in MASON Cycles’ obsession with high-performance steel, welded by one of the most skilled and established steel bicycle frame builders in Italy - Cicli Barco.\n\nSimply stunning from every aspect, thanks to exceptional ride quality and attention to detail that sets it above the rest. In my opinion, it's faultless.\n\nRoad.cc ROAD BIKE OF THE YEAR AND OVERALL WINNER - BIKE OF THE YEAR 2022/23\n\nThe SLR tubeset makes for an engaging and comfortable ride with an emphasis on smooth, fast travel. The custom shaped, progressively-butted, phosphate-coated Dedacciai Zero/Zero Uno tube set is made exclusively for the SLR frame. It offers class-leading compliance and weight, combined with a propulsive, plush ride quality, and maximum pedalling efficiency.\n\nPaired with a new MASON full-carbon fork, the RangeFinder AR [AllRoad] – which is tuned for all-conditions riding on firmer surfaces with large tyres. The RangeFinder AR features a set of molded-in eyelets which are designed to be fitted with a front rack or rando-style bag support, in addition to an internally-routed dynamo front light.\n\nThe SLR has capacity for 700C x 40mm tyres, including full mudguards and multiple attachment points for accessories and carriers. This gives the SLR wide-ranging all-condition, and long-distance capability – from refined grand-touring to fast cross-country and multi-day adventures.\n\n1-1/8” - 1.5” tapered Dedacciai Zero Uno headtube with integrated Deda headset\n\n100% Italian TIG-welded/silver-brazed frame manufacturing, wet-painting and finishing\n\nExclusive MASON TiltShift precision-aligned UK-made BEAR dropouts, featuring a clockable stainless steel insert to enable absolute accuracy in alignment\n\nDiscreet pump peg behind head tube to securely fit a full-size frame pump\n\nDiscreet internal dynamo-light routing in top-tube with stainless-steel port reinforcement as standard\n\nChain pip neatly holds the chain and retains it on the chainring whilst the wheel is removed for transport.\n\nSilver-brazed and threaded rear rack bosses.\n\nBottle cage/Accessory cage boss placements as standard: x2 inside the front triangle; x1 underneath down tube.\n\nFully internal gear and brake routing as standard. Exit for Di2/EPS on seat tube with stainless steel reinforcement as standard.\n\nClearance for 50/34T double chainrings.\n\nDedacciai Zero Uno seat tube with flush-fitting alloy reduction sleeve for 27.2mm seat post.",
